{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFollow-up to the `scanner-integration` incident and ticket `90c7-c465-4037-42d5`.\nThe original plan included guarding `.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml`, but that workflow\nand `scripts/install_review_scanners.py` are absent from current `origin/main` after revert\n`9c7d78127696`. This ticket therefore does **not** recreate or re-land the scanner lane. The\nscanner lane re-land is owned by a separate later ticket.\n\nTwo general-purpose hardening gaps still exist on main:\n\n1. `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` keeps a hardcoded workflow tuple. That lets a\n   newly wired reusable workflow escape the predates-gate guard invariant until someone remembers to\n   add it to the tuple.\n2. `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` does not statically reject bash-only constructs inside\n   make recipes reached from the CI workflows. A parse-only `dash -n` check is insufficient because\n   dash validates `set -o pipefail` at runtime, not parse time. This leaves a class where a lane can\n   vote green without actually executing the recipe it claims to verify.\n\nADR 0114 applies to new required CI gates. This ticket only strengthens unit tests exercised by the\nexisting suite; it does not add or promote a CI voting lane.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. In `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`, derive `GUARDED_WORKFLOWS` from the local\n   `uses:` transitive closure rooted at `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` and\n   `.github/workflows/test.yml`. Keep the former hardcoded workflow list as a required floor and\n   assert the derived set is a superset, so any reusable workflow wired into the gating/mirror lanes\n   enters the predates-gate guard invariant immediately, including a future scanner lane re-land.\n2. In `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`, add a static text scan over every CI-reachable make\n   recipe and fail on non-POSIX-dash constructs: `set -o pipefail`, `[[ ... ]]`, indexed or\n   associative arrays, here-strings `<<<`, and `${var^}` / `${var,}` case-modification. The check is\n   intentionally static-text based rather than relying only on `dash -n`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` derives `GUARDED_WORKFLOWS` from the\n      `gerrit-verify.yaml` / `test.yml` local `uses:` transitive closure and asserts the existing\n      guard list remains a floor. A seeded omission or newly wired reusable workflow must fail the\n      predates-gate guard coverage test.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` statically scans CI-reachable make recipes for\n      bash-only constructs (`set -o pipefail`, `[[ ... ]]`, arrays, `<<<`, `${var^}`, `${var,}`)\n      instead of relying on parse-only `dash -n`; seeding `set -o pipefail` into a reachable recipe\n      must fail naming the offending construct and recipe.\n- [ ] No scanner workflow or scanner install script is recreated, and no new required CI voting lane\n      is added. This ticket stays limited to unit-test coverage for the two surviving invariants.\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED/held-out oracle: strengthen the two unit-test modules first, then confirm they fail for the\n  correct reason against current implementation (hardcoded guarded workflow set; missing static scan\n  for a seeded bash-only construct).\n- GREEN: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py -q`\n- Mutation teeth: temporarily reintroduce the escaped defects (hardcoded/omitted guarded workflow\n  coverage and `set -o pipefail` in a reachable recipe) and confirm the oracle goes RED, then restore.\n- Local gates: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and\n  `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788571358134219001,"uuid":"ab3c71ca-7a83-4f39-8144-27c9faaa20fe"}